_yesterday/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/denmark_yesterday.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,990\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Yesterday single artwork \u2013 Denmark\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/denmark_yesterday-960x950.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/brazil_yesterday_ep/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/brazil_yesterday_ep-200x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Yesterday EP artwork - Brazil\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/brazil_yesterday_ep-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/brazil_yesterday_ep-580x576.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/brazil_yesterday_ep-960x953.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/brazil_yesterday_ep-768x763.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/brazil_yesterday_ep-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/brazil_yesterday_ep.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"9197\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/brazil_yesterday_ep/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/brazil_yesterday_ep.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,993\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Yesterday EP artwork \u2013 Brazil\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/brazil_yesterday_ep-960x953.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/mexico_yesterday_ep/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/mexico_yesterday_ep-200x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Yesterday EP artwork - Mexico\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/mexico_yesterday_ep-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/mexico_yesterday_ep-580x580.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/mexico_yesterday_ep-960x960.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/mexico_yesterday_ep-768x767.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/mexico_yesterday_ep-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/mexico_yesterday_ep.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"9780\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/mexico_yesterday_ep/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/mexico_yesterday_ep.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,999\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Yesterday EP artwork \u2013 Mexico\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/mexico_yesterday_ep-960x960.jpg\" /></a></div></figure></div><p>In 1980 John Lennon explained how he was often mistakenly credited with having written the song.</p><blockquote><div>I go to restaurants and the groups always play &#8216;Yesterday&#8217;. <a href=\"/people/yoko-ono/\">Yoko</a> and I even signed a guy&#8217;s violin in Spain after he played us &#8216;Yesterday&#8217;. He couldn&#8217;t understand that I didn&#8217;t write the song. But I guess he couldn&#8217;t have gone from table to table playing <a href=\"/songs/i-am-the-walrus/\">&#8216;I Am The Walrus&#8217;</a>.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">John Lennon, 1980<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/allwearesaying\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>All We Are Saying</em></a>, David Sheff</div><p>In the same interview Lennon spoke of McCartney&#8217;s skills as a lyricist.</p><blockquote><div>A couple of lines he&#8217;s come up with show indications he&#8217;s a good lyricist, but he just never took it anywhere. He wrote the lyrics to &#8216;Yesterday&#8217;. Although the lyrics don&#8217;t resolve into any sense, they&#8217;re <em>good</em> lines. They certainly work. You know what I mean? They&#8217;re good \u2013 but if you read the whole song, it doesn&#8217;t <em>say</em> anything; you don&#8217;t know what happened. She left and he wishes it was yesterday \u2013 that much you get \u2013 but it doesn&#8217;t really resolve. So, mine didn&#8217;t use to resolve, either\u2026</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">John Lennon<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/allwearesaying\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>All We Are Saying</em></a>, David Sheff</div><p>&#8216;Yesterday&#8217; was issued as a US single on <a href=\"/1965/09/13/us-single-yesterday/\">13 September 1965</a>. Newspapers at the time commentated that &#8220;Paul McCartney is number one without the other Beatles&#8221;. It swiftly became the most-played song on American radio, a position it held for eight consecutive years.</p><p>There were also a number of single and EP releases of the song. In the UK it was the title track of The Beatles&#8217; 11th EP, released on <a href=\"/1966/03/04/uk-ep-yesterday/\">4 March 1966</a>, although it was not a single in their home country.</p><p>Since its release there have been over 3,000 cover versions of &#8216;Yesterday&#8217;.</p><blockquote><div>It&#8217;s still strange to me when people tell me things like &#8216;Yesterday&#8217; is the number one pop song of all time. Apparently, <em>Rolling Stone</em> described it as the best song of the twentieth century. It all seems quite grand for something that came into the world so mysteriously.</p><p>Some people find it hard to believe that I was twenty-two when I wrote &#8216;Yesterday&#8217;. Every time I come to the line &#8216;I&#8217;m not half the man I used to be&#8217;, I remember I&#8217;d lost my mother about eight years before that. It&#8217;s been suggested to me that this is a &#8216;losing my mother&#8217; song, to which I&#8217;ve always said, &#8216;No, I don&#8217;t believe so.&#8217; But, you know, the more I think about it\u00a0\u2013 &#8216;Why she had to go I don&#8217;t know, she wouldn&#8217;t say&#8217; \u2013\u00a0I can see that that might have been part of the background, the unconsciousness behind this song after all. It was so strange that the loss of our mother to cancer was simply not discussed. We barely knew what cancer was, but I&#8217;m now not surprised that the whole experience surfaced in this song where sweetness competes with a pain you can&#8217;t quite describe.</p><p>A while back, someone asked me whether I relate differently to my songs as I grow older. A recording doesn&#8217;t age, but of course we continue to age and grow, and as you get older, your relationship to a song can grow too. When I wrote &#8216;Yesterday&#8217;, I had just moved to London from Liverpool, and I was starting to see a whole new world of possibilities open up before me. But all my yesterdays covered a pretty small period at that point. Now the song seems even more significant \u2013\u00a0yes, more poignant \u2013\u00a0because of the time that has passed since I wrote it. I must admit, that&#8217;s an aspect of writing songs and playing music that I really like.</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Paul McCartney<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/mccartneylyrics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>The Lyrics: 1956 To The Present</em></a></div><div class=\"fab-forum-link\"><a href=\"/fab-forum/the-songs/yesterday/\">Discuss &#8216;Yesterday&#8217; on the Fab Forum \u00bb</a></div><div class=\"wp-post-navigation\"><div class=\"wp-post-navigation-pre\"> <strong>Previous song:</strong> <a href=\"/songs/ive-just-seen-a-face/\">&#8216;I&#8217;ve Just Seen A Face&#8217;</a></div><div class=\"wp-post-navigation-next\"> <strong>Next song:</strong> <a href=\"/songs/dizzy-miss-lizzy/\">&#8216;Dizzy Miss Lizzy&#8217;</a></div></div><div align=\"center\" style=\"clear:both;margin:15px 0;\"></div><div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/songs/yesterday/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></a> <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></span></div>",
